{%- comment -%}
  Bassface legal pages — the boards are `dtbGV` Privacy, `FsLJt` Refund,
  `Lb6aG` Shipping, `pnQNk` Terms, `pukrO` Contact Information,
  `D9kj1` Partial Payment and `ZwHbP` Privacy Choices, all at 1440.

  ONE SECTION, ONE TEMPLATE, SEVEN PAGES. Shopify has no policy template type,
  so the store's /policies/* URLs cannot carry this design at all — every legal
  page here is an ordinary Page assigned the `Legal` template by hand, under
  Online Store > Pages > … > Theme template, exactly as About is. The footer
  already knows: bf-footer.liquid switches to its minimal variant on
  `template.suffix == 'legal'`.

  THE COPY LIVES IN THE PAGE, NOT IN SETTINGS, and it has to. Seven pages share
  this one template, so anything stored in section settings or blocks would be
  stored ONCE and appear identically on all seven. `page.content` is the only
  per-page surface there is, which makes the page editor the single place a
  policy is ever edited — and the right place, since these are documents a
  lawyer amends, not a layout a designer arranges.

  The consequence is that the design's section pattern — the `01` numeral, the
  hairline, the block types — has to be reachable from what the rich text editor
  produces. It is, entirely in CSS: see the authoring contract in
  bf-main-legal.css, which is the file to read before touching any of this. The
  numerals are counters, so they renumber themselves when a section is added or
  removed. Nothing on this page stores a number.

  NO REVEAL ON THE INDEX, deliberately. bf-page-transition swaps the whole of
  <main> on a policy-to-policy click, so every <bf-reveal> inside it is a fresh
  element that animates again. On the title that is right — it is the thing that
  changed. On the index it would be wrong twice over: the column the visitor is
  aiming at would jump under the cursor, and the one part of the page that is
  supposed to feel bolted down would be the part that moves.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'bf-breadcrumb.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-reveal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-legal-index.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-main-legal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'bf-reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign updated = page.metafields.custom.last_updated

  if updated.type == 'date' or updated.type == 'date_time'
    assign updated_text = updated.value | date: '%-d %B %Y'
  else
    assign updated_text = updated.value
  endif
-%}

<div class="legal">
  {%- render 'bf-breadcrumb',
    current: page.title,
    home_label: section.settings.breadcrumb_home,
    label: section.settings.breadcrumb_label
  -%}

  <div class="legal__header">
    <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
      <h1 class="legal__title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    </bf-reveal>

    {%- comment -%}
      "Last updated" is a page metafield rather than a setting for the same
      reason the body is: a setting would give all seven pages one date, and the
      one thing a visitor checks on a policy is whether it changed since they
      last read it. Absent on a page that has never set it, which is correct —
      an invented date is worse than none.

      Definition to create: custom.last_updated, type Date, on Pages.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if updated_text != blank -%}
      <p class="legal__updated">
        {{- section.settings.updated_label }}
        {{ updated_text -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="legal__body">
    {%- render 'bf-legal-index',
      menu: section.settings.index_menu,
      heading: section.settings.index_heading,
      label: section.settings.index_label
    -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      `page.content` is already sanitised HTML from the page editor, so it is
      output raw — an `escape` here would print the markup as text.

      The wrapper is what the counters are scoped to and what the swap fades in,
      so it stays even when the page is empty.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="legal__doc">{{ page.content }}</div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Legal page",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Title and body come from the page itself — this template is shared by every legal page, so anything set here shows on all of them."
    },
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "index_menu",
      "label": "Legal menu",
      "info": "The index down the side. Point it at Pages, not /policies/ URLs. The current page is marked automatically. Suggested menu: legal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "index_heading",
      "label": "Index eyebrow",
      "default": "LEGAL"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "index_label",
      "label": "Index landmark name",
      "info": "Read by screen readers to announce the navigation. Not shown.",
      "default": "Legal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "updated_label",
      "label": "Last updated prefix",
      "info": "Shown only on pages with a custom.last_updated metafield, followed by the date.",
      "default": "Last updated"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "breadcrumb_home",
      "label": "Breadcrumb home link",
      "default": "Home"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "breadcrumb_label",
      "label": "Breadcrumb landmark name",
      "info": "Read by screen readers to announce the navigation. Not shown.",
      "default": "Breadcrumb"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
